      "content": "ugh man, a grounded plane right before the peak long-haul window is gonna be a nightmare. the ops team is already breathing down my neck about the revenue loss if we pull this one out of rotation. looking closer at the data you flagged... the spikes are really incremental. is there any chance these are just sensor noise or thermal expansion transients from the last leg? seems like a lot of hassle for what might just be a calibration quirk.",
